# Ben's Pizza Parlor, the pack in words (content-pizza: pizza-pack, 2026-11-08)

`packs/pizza/pack.js` (pack version 1), the pilot restaurant on the ladder and **the worked example of slots** for
phase 2b (the diner, `docs/api/packs/diner.md`, uses the Burger Bar's own `from`/`of` picks). Format:
`docs/api/pack-format.md`; the line `docs/api/line.md`; the script `docs/api/script.md`; sounds `docs/api/audio.md`;
the food `docs/api/world.md`. **food-pizza works from section 10** (every look, set, flourish and cook to draw).
**pizza-script works from section 12** (every moment and who must say it).

**Check it** (from the game folder):

```
BB_PACKS=pizza node --test "tests/*.test.cjs"
node -e "console.table(require('./tests/bot.cjs').pressReport('pizza'))"
node -e "const b=require('./tests/bot.cjs'); console.log(b.schema.validate(b.merge(require('./packs/pizza/pack.js'))))"
```

## 1. At a glance

| | |
|---|---|
| id, name | `pizza`, "Ben's Pizza Parlor" (court: "Pizza Parlor", bottom arm, slot 1, open at the start) |
| version | 1 |
| format | not set: pizza-script sets `format: 3` when `packs/pizza/script.js` covers every moment |
| manager | `{ id: 'mitch', art: 'mitch-pizza' }`: flour-dusted apron, pizza-box hat |
| backdrops | `counter`, and by station `prep` (prep, cut, knotBasket) and `oven` (oven). All three exist (`BBArt.pizza`) |
| courses | `['main', 'side']`: pizzas are mains, garlic knots the side |
| levels | `{}`: the engine's ladder unchanged |
| no paging | every pick has 3 values, so no screen ever shows More… (a gross-out could sit on any of them) |

## 2. The line: stations and steps

| Station | backdrop | Steps, in order | redo | tool | sounds |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `prep` "Prep Table" | `prep` | builds on `pizza` (no base: the crust is a pick). Pick `crust` → auto `toss` (show `doughToss`) → Pick `sauce` → Add, one each: cheese, pepperoni, sausage, mushrooms, peppers, onions, olives, pineapple | "Redo the Pizza" | | (add: `plop`) |
| `oven` "Oven" | `oven` | Cook, stage set `bake` (cooks the item: the pizza, or the knots) | "Bake Again" | `peel` | `{ cook: 'oven', done: 'peel' }` |
| `cut` "Cutting Board" | `prep` | Pick `slices` | "Cut Again" | | `{ done: 'cut' }` |
| `knotBasket` "Knot Basket" | `prep` | Add garlic butter → Add parmesan → Pick `dip` | "Redo the Knots" | | (add: `plop`) |

A pizza runs prep → oven → cut; garlic knots run oven → knotBasket (baked first, then dressed). No `when` steps: every
pizza is asked every step, so every pizza takes the same presses whatever is on it.

What the player hears (words.js; Timed changes only the oven):

- "Prep Table. Crust: Thin, Regular or Deep Dish?" → the dough toss plays → "Sauce: Red, White or None?" → "Cheese."
  Add / Skip ("Add cheese"), then "Pepperoni.", "Sausage." … "Pineapple.". A bad one: "Pepperoni with a fly on it."
  Add / Skip / Swap It ("Swap pepperoni with a fly on it for a fresh one").
- "Oven. How baked?" Light / Golden / Crispy. Timed: "Oven. Pull it out when it is right.", one button **Pull It Out**
  (said "Pull it out. Golden"); left in, it stops at Burnt.
- "Cutting Board. Slices: 4, 6 or 8?" 4 / 6 / 8.
- "Knot Basket. Garlic butter." Add / Skip, "Parmesan." Add / Skip, "Dip: Marinara, Ranch or Pesto?".
- Review: "Here it is." Ring It Up, the redo words, or Redo… (a row) when there are more than three.

**Toppings are Add steps, not a repeat pick.** The task text said "a repeat pick with Done"; spec 5.3 says "toppings
one at a time", the proposal "toppings one at a time, Add or Skip", and DESIGN.md "the ingredients come to him". I
followed the spec and the proposal, because a repeat pick cannot do what the same task asks: a repeat can't carry a
gross-out (the fly on the pepperoni and the mouldy mushrooms sit on toppings), `dislikes` are ingredient ids (Oakes's
onions and Tony's pineapple are held only as recipe parts), a repeat needs at least one pick (no plain cheese pizza),
and 7 values page with More…, so a topping would be hunted for instead of coming down the line. The press budget holds
without it (section 16): every pizza is 13, the worst order 26.

## 3. Cooking: one stage set

| set | stages (first .. last) | Simple `choose` | ask | stop | speed |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `bake` | raw, light, golden, crispy, burnt | Light, Golden, Crispy | "How baked?" | "Pull It Out" | pack `cookSpeeds` 12 / 8 / 5 s a stage, `wantedScale` 2 (the Burger Bar's grill) |

Stage names: Raw, Light, Golden, Crispy, Burnt. **Burnt crust is Timed's last stage** (one mistake, `complain.done`),
never a gross-out. Pizzas and knots both cook to the recipe's `done: { pick: 'bake' }` (normal Golden).

## 4. Recipes

`level` is the only gate. Prices are the tip's base. "As written" is the ticket with the normal picks (change 0).

| id | Name | level | course | stations | price | As written (the ticket) | Can change |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `cheesePizza` | Cheese Pizza | 1 | main | prep, oven, cut | 8 | regular crust, red sauce, with cheese, golden, 8 slices | crust, sauce, bake, slices; adds mushrooms, olives |
| `pepperoniPizza` | Pepperoni Pizza | 1 | main | prep, oven, cut | 9 | …with cheese and pepperoni… | picks; adds mushrooms, peppers, onions |
| `veggiePizza` | Veggie Pizza | 2 | main | prep, oven, cut | 10 | …with cheese, mushrooms, peppers, onions and olives… | picks; holds onions, olives |
| `meatLovers` | Meat Lover's Pizza | 2 | main | prep, oven, cut | 11 | …with cheese, pepperoni and sausage… | picks; adds onions |
| `hawaiian` | Hawaiian Pizza | 2 | main | prep, oven, cut | 10 | …with cheese, pepperoni and pineapple… | picks; holds pepperoni |
| `garlicKnots` | Garlic Knots (plural "Baskets of Garlic Knots") | 2 | side | oven, knotBasket | 4 | golden, with garlic butter and parmesan, marinara dip | bake, dip; holds butter, parmesan |
| `everythingPizza` | Everything Pizza | 3 | main | prep, oven, cut | 13 | …with cheese, pepperoni, sausage, mushrooms, peppers, onions, olives and pineapple… | picks; holds mushrooms, peppers, onions, olives, pineapple |
| `heartPizza` | Heart-Shaped Pizza | `'event'` | main | prep, oven, cut | 24 | regular crust, red sauce, with cheese and pepperoni, golden, 8 slices; `look: { shape: 'heartPizza', giant: true }` | the finale only |

Slots and picks (level 5 uses the fancy lists):

| slot (question) | values (label; ticket words) | pick: values, normal, fancy |
|---|---|---|
| `crust` "Crust" | thin "Thin", regular "Regular", deepDish "Deep Dish"; "thin crust" | thin/regular/deepDish, regular |
| `sauce` "Sauce" | red "Red", white "White", noSauce "None"; "red sauce", "sauce: none" (never "no sauce") | red/white, red, fancy + noSauce |
| `slices` "Slices" | four "4", six "6", eight "8"; "8 slices" | four/six/eight, eight |
| `dip` "Dip" | marinara, ranch, pesto; "marinara dip" | marinara/ranch, marinara, fancy + pesto |

**Combos** (level 3 up): one item, or two at the level's `more` odds: a pizza and garlic knots, in that order. Never
two pizzas except Gus's two of one thing. Order Size "One Item" makes every order one item.

## 5. The ladder (`levels: {}`)

| Level | On offer | Items | Gross-outs | Extras |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | cheese, pepperoni | 1; at most 2 optional toppings; change 0.2 | none | |
| 2 | + veggie, meat lover's, hawaiian, garlic knots | 1; change 0.3 | none | |
| 3 | + everything | 1 or 2 (35% two): pizza + knots | 0.3 an order, at most 2 a shift, never the first | |
| 4 | the same | as 3, change 0.4 | as 3 | one odd order at 50% a shift; one visitor (Reginald, Kai or Breeze), never first |
| 5 | the same | as 4, change 0.5, fancy (None sauce, pesto) | 0.35, at most 2 | odd orders at 60%, `allTheWay` too |

Measured over 300 five-order shifts a level: levels 3-5 serve about 35% two-item orders; the gross-outs land on the
cheese (hair) about twice as often as the pepperoni (fly), and the mushrooms (mouldy) least, as the menu has them.

## 6. Ridiculous orders (level 4 and 5)

The customer says `order.odd.<id>` instead of the order; the ticket is plain and complete. At most one a shift, never
the first order or the visitor's.

| id | level | recipe | the change | The ticket | Who | Presses |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `justCrust` | 4 | cheesePizza | holds cheese; sauce None | Cheese Pizza: regular crust, sauce: none, nothing else on it, golden, 8 slices | anyone | 13 |
| `halfAndHalf` | 4 | pepperoniPizza | adds pineapple ("half pepperoni, half pineapple and anchovies" is said: no halves, no anchovies) | Pepperoni Pizza: …with cheese, pepperoni and pineapple… | not Tony | 13 |
| `heartShaped` | 4 | pepperoniPizza | none: "heart-shaped, I'm proposing" is said; only the event's giant is a heart | Pepperoni Pizza: …golden, 8 slices | anyone | 13 |
| `allTheWay` | 5 | everythingPizza | deep dish, crispy, 4 slices ("everything, all the way") | Everything Pizza: deep dish crust, red sauce, with cheese, pepperoni, sausage, mushrooms, peppers, onions, olives and pineapple, crispy, 4 slices | anyone (dislikes still held) | 13 |

## 7. The five-star event: The Pizza Party

```js
events: { five: { name: 'The Pizza Party',
  customers: ['marge', 'gus', 'bev', 'vernon', 'sal', 'oakes', 'tony', 'reginald', 'kai'],
  finale: { customer: 'pam', items: [{ recipe: 'heartPizza', set: { bake: 'golden' } },
    { recipe: 'garlicKnots', set: { bake: 'golden', dip: 'marinara' } }] } } }
```

- A wedding party, **spoken of, never shown**: the guests are the drawn cast; Pam orders for the wedding party (her
  `order.gag`). Shift Length orders at level-4 complexity, no visitors, no odd orders.
- The finale, always last: "Heart-Shaped Pizza: regular crust, red sauce, with cheese and pepperoni, golden, 8
  slices. Garlic Knots: golden, with garlic butter and parmesan, marinara dip." 17 presses. The heart is drawn giant
  and adds no choices. If Pam isn't drawn, the first drawn regular (Marge) orders it.
- Mitch: `event.intro`, `event.celebrate`, `event.again`.

