## 9. Gross-outs (from level 3; all on prep's Add steps)

| id | on | label (`say`) | fx (all the kit's) | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `hair` | cheese | "{name} with a hair in it" → "Cheese with a hair in it." | `hair` | Mitch `gross.hair`; served: `react.gross`, `complain.gross.hair` |
| `mouldy` | mushrooms | "the mouldy {name}" → "The mouldy mushrooms." | `spots` (#6d8c3a, 9), `tint` #9c9670, `stink` | as above, `.mouldy` |
| `fly` | pepperoni | "{name} with a fly on it" | `fly` (game.js plays `buzz` for the id `fly`) | as above, `.fly` |

Swap It replaces it and asks again; Skip sends it back (a missing-topping mistake if the ticket wanted it). Burnt crust
is Timed's last stage instead (spec 4.6). The receipt says e.g. "Mushrooms: mouldy mushrooms".

## 10. For food-pizza: every look, set, flourish and cook

`made()` of a pizza: `{ recipe, ing: 'pizza', done: 'golden', parts: [{ ing: 'cheese' }, { ing: 'pepperoni', gross? }],
gross, picks: { crust, sauce, slices }, counts: {}, auto: ['toss'] }`. `k.sequence` gives vessel `pizza` (the pan) and
the parts in line order: the crust value, the sauce value, cheese, the toppings, then (after the cut) the slices value.
Garlic knots: `{ recipe: 'garlicKnots', ing: 'knots', done, parts: [garlicButter, parmesan], picks: { dip } }`: body
`knots` at `made.done`, then the butter, parmesan and the dip value. **Recipe looks name the layout**: read
`pack.recipes[made.recipe].look.shape` in `layoutOf` (`pizza`, `heartPizza`, `knotBasket`); the kit's `stack` would
pile toppings up, a pizza spreads them out.

| look.shape | used by | set(s) | how it looks | with cooking (`made.done`, or `o.stage` in the oven) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `pizzaPan` | ingredient `pizza` (the vessel) | prep, oven, counter | a round steel pan a little wider than the crust; a deep straight-sided pan when `made.picks.crust` is `deepDish` | none; the look's `ramp` is the oven dial's swatches |
| `thinCrust` | crust `thin` | prep, oven, counter | a thin flat dough disc, a narrow low rim | pale dough (raw) → light → golden → crispy brown → burnt dark: the pack's `pizza` ramp |
| `regularCrust` | crust `regular` | " | a medium disc with a puffy rounded rim | the same ramp |
| `deepDishCrust` | crust `deepDish` | " | a tall-sided crust filling the deep pan | the same ramp, the rim darkest |
| `pizzaSauce` | sauce `red` (#c8321f), `white` (#f7efdc) | " | a sauce layer inside the rim, `look.colour` | a little darker at crispy, darker at burnt |
| `bareDough` | sauce `noSauce` | " | no sauce: a few white flour specks on the bare dough face, so "sauce: none" looks bare | none (the crust browns under it) |
| `mozzarella` | cheese | " | shredded white cheese spread inside the rim | shreds (raw) → melted smooth (light) → golden-brown spots (golden) → browned blisters (crispy) → charred patches (burnt) |
| `pepperoni` | pepperoni | " | about 12 red discs with dark flecks, scattered | the edges cup up and darken |
| `sausage` | sausage | " | about 14 brown crumbles | darker brown |
| `mushrooms` | mushrooms | " | about 10 sliced mushroom profiles (cap and stem), tan | shrink a little, darker edges |
| `greenPeppers` | peppers | " | about 10 green strips and crescents | char flecks at crispy and burnt |
| `redOnions` | onions | " | thin purple-red slivers | softer, browned tips |
| `blackOlives` | olives | " | about 12 black rings | none |
| `pineapple` | pineapple | " | about 10 yellow chunks | caramelised edges at crispy |
| `pizzaCut` | slices `four`/`six`/`eight` (`look.slices`) | prep (the cut), counter | that many radial cut grooves across the whole pizza, the wedges a hair apart, on top of everything | none (cut after the oven) |
| `garlicKnots` | ingredient `knots` (the body) | oven, prep, counter | six knotted dough rolls in a heap | raw pale → light → golden → crispy → burnt: the pack's `knots` ramp |
| `garlicButter` | garlic butter | prep (knot basket), counter | a glossy yellow glaze on the knots with green parsley and garlic flecks; waits in a little pot with a brush | none (added after the oven) |
| `parmesan` | parmesan | " | a fine pale dusting over the knots; waits in a shaker (the kit's `shake` fits) | none |
| `dipCup` | dip `marinara` (#b8301f), `ranch` (#f4f1e6), `pesto` (#5f8f2e) | " | a small fluted paper cup of dip, `look.colour`, set beside the knots | none |
| `pizza` | recipe look: every pizza but the heart | layout | the round pizza: pan, crust, sauce, cheese, then each topping scattered evenly inside the rim (its own seeded scatter, so toppings don't pile in one spot), cut lines on top | by `made.done` |
| `heartPizza` | recipe look of `heartPizza`, `giant: true` | layout | the pizza layout with a heart-shaped crust, sauce and cheese, the pepperoni as little hearts, the cut lines following the heart; the kit draws it 1.6 times bigger (cap it on prep with `giantMax`) | as `pizza` |
| `knotBasket` | recipe look of `garlicKnots` | layout | a red-and-white checkered paper basket holding the knots, the dip cup beside it | by `made.done` |

Toppings waiting on the line (`incoming`) are a small heap of that topping in a steel topping tin; on the pizza they
scatter over the cheese (read `o.below()` for the radius; keep `h` small so every topping lands on the same surface).

**Sets** (measure your own lines: the 5.2 table asked for prep 62 and oven 65; the counter keeps the diner's fixed camera,
`line: null`):

- `counter`: the diner's counter camera and top height, red-and-white colours; `counter.arrange` puts a pizza and the
  knots basket side by side (two pizzas side by side, shrunk to fit).
- `prep`: the pan low and left of centre (`stack`), the next topping on the right (`incoming`), `giantMax` for the heart.
  Its `pick` hook: a `slices` pick rolls a pizza wheel across, then the cut lines show; a `dip` pick sets the cup down.
  Its `auto` (or the module's `autos`): **`doughToss`**, after the crust pick: the dough spins up off the table,
  stretches in the air and lands as the chosen crust (Reduced: it lands at once).
- `oven`: the brick oven's mouth (`cook: 'oven'`): the item (`s.made`: a pizza, or the knots) slides in on the peel;
  `show(c, s)` draws it at `s.stage`; Simple's `run` bakes to the chosen stage and slides it out; Timed: the cheese
  bubbles (`k.spin` bubble), the crust darkens a stage at a time, smoke puffs at burnt. **Doneness shows as a colour
  and a mark** (e.g. blister or char marks counted by stage). The Timed control prop is the page's `peel`.

Gross-out fx are the kit's (`hair`, `fly`, `spots`, `tint`, `stink`): no custom fx.

## 11. Sounds

`oven` station: `cook: 'oven'` (the pizza slides in), `done: 'peel'` (it comes out); `cut`: `done: 'cut'` (the wheel
rolls). Every Add plays the default `plop`, each Timed stage `tick`. The page plays `swoosh` (Skip), `toss` (Swap It),
`buzz` (the gross-out id `fly`), `ding`, `kaching`, `stars`, `ew` as for the diner. All exist (`packs/pizza/sound`,
`packs/shared/sound`); `tests/voices.test.cjs` checks them. The dough toss has no sound (no shared sound fits; Skip's
`swoosh` would muddle that cue).

## 12. For pizza-script: every moment and who must say it

`SC.moments(pack)` on the merged pack, 265 coverage items with an empty script. F = the pack's 'customer' fallback
lines count for anyone with fewer than two of their own.

- **Customers, everyone** (marge gus bev vernon sal oakes tony pam reginald kai breeze): `greet` ×3, `smalltalk` ×3,
  `goodbye` ×3 (the cast script may supply these three); F: `react.3`/`.2`/`.1` ×3, `react.gross`,
  `complain.extra`/`.unasked`/`.missing` ({ing}{ings}), `complain.done` ({want}{got}: stage words), `complain.pick`
  ({slot}{want}{got}{value}), `complain.more`, `complain.gross.hair`/`.mouldy`/`.fly` ({ing}{ings}).
- **Some**: `visitor.arrive` reginald kai breeze; `order.usual` marge; `order.twin` gus; `order.dislike` oakes, tony
  ({ing}{ings}); `order.gag` tony, pam (locals at home; ≤ 8 s); `react.favourite` bev, sal; F `order.odd.justCrust`,
  `.heartShaped`, `.allTheWay` (marge gus bev vernon sal oakes tony pam) and `.halfAndHalf` (not tony).
- **Mitch** (2 each unless 1): `shift.start`, `shift.end`, `uniform` (1); `tutorial.intro`, `.ticket`, `.review`,
  `.serve`, `.gross`; `tutorial.prep`, `.oven`, `.cut`, `.knotBasket`, `tutorial.cook.oven`;
  `tutorial.warn.extra`/`.unasked`/`.missing`/`.done`/`.pick`/`.gross`/`.grossSkip`; `gross.hair`, `.mouldy`, `.fly`;
  `nearly` ({want}{name}), `after.3`, `after.1`, `after.gross`, `event.intro`/`.celebrate`/`.again` ({name}) (1).
- **Not needed**: `complain.tooMany`/`.tooFew` and their warnings (no Add with a max above 1, no repeat).
- **Blank words**: {slot} crust, sauce, slices, dip; {want}/{got} thin, regular, deep dish, red, white, **none**, 4, 6,
  8, marinara, ranch, pesto; stages light, golden, crispy, raw, burnt; {ing} pizza or garlic knots for `done`.
  "I said {want} {slot}" reads "I said none sauce" for a None sauce: write pick lines that work for every slot, e.g.
  "The ticket said {slot}: {want}." ("sauce: none", "slices: 8").
- **The brief**: Tony's gag is pineapple and purism; Pam's "for twelve" (and the wedding party at the event); Gus's
  "two larges" (`order.twin`); Vernon "I will know"; Oakes's onion reason; Breeze (a visitor here) loves the Hawaiian;
  the odd orders as in section 6.

## 13. Help

"Ben's Pizza Parlor. Every pizza starts at the prep table: pick the crust, then the sauce, then Add or Skip the cheese
and each topping as it comes down the line. Then the oven: in Simple, pick how baked it is, Light, Golden or Crispy; in
Timed, watch it bake and Pull It Out when it reaches the stage on the ticket. Last, the cutting board: pick how many
slices. Garlic knots bake in the same oven, then get their garlic butter, parmesan and dip at the knot basket. The
ticket lists everything: add what's on it, skip what isn't. If something looks wrong, Swap It brings a fresh one."

