## 15. The tutorial

Tony (the parlor's own); one guided order through every station: "Pepperoni Pizza: regular crust, red sauce, with
cheese and pepperoni, golden, 8 slices. Garlic Knots: golden, with garlic butter and parmesan, marinara dip." The
pepperoni comes down with a fly on it (`gross: { item: 0, ing: 'pepperoni', event: 'fly' }`), so Swap It is taught
once. Always Simple; Mitch warns before each mistake. 17 presses done right, plus the Swap It: 18.

## 16. Press counts (`pressReport('pizza')`, Serve included; Simple and Timed alike, the same at every level)

| recipe | levels | presses |
|---|---|---|
| cheesePizza, pepperoniPizza | 1-5 | 13 (crust, sauce, cheese, 7 toppings, oven, slices, Serve) |
| veggiePizza, meatLovers, hawaiian | 2-5 | 13 |
| garlicKnots | 2-5 | 5 (oven, butter, parmesan, dip, Serve) |
| everythingPizza | 3-5 | 13 |
| heartPizza (event) | event | 13 alone; the finale with knots 17 |

Whole orders (bots, both modes): level 1 and 2 at most 13; levels 3-5 and the event at most 26 (Gus's two pizzas,
25, plus a Swap It); a pizza with knots 17; two knots 9; every odd order 13; the tutorial 18. Budget (spec 4.3): level
1 ≤ 14, any order ≤ 28. No order can hold three pizzas (combos are one a course; the finale is two items).

## 17. Requests (for the owners named)

- **integrate / page**: load `packs/pizza/pack.js` (and `packs/pizza/script.js` once written) and `js/food/pizza.js`.
- **page**: draw the `peel` as the oven's Timed control (a button labelled "Pull It Out" until then); play the `auto`
  event `doughToss` after the crust pick; theme tokens as diner.md 14 lists them (the contrast above assumes it).
- **food-pizza**: section 10. **pizza-script**: section 12, then `format: 3` in the pack.
